# Mosquitto ACL file
#
# Restricts each authenticated MQTT user to the minimum topic access it
# actually needs. Referenced by docker/mosquitto.conf via `acl_file`.
#
# Usernames here are fixed (not operator-configurable) and must match
# exactly what docker-compose.yml's mosquitto service generates into the
# password file at container start - one user per agent TYPE, plus
# "edge_gateway" for the gateway process. Passwords come from
# MOSQUITTO_PASSWORD (edge_gateway) and MOSQUITTO_AGENT_PASSWORD (shared by
# all five agent-type users) in docker/.env.
#
# NOTE: this scopes to agent TYPE, not physical device - any two PLC agents
# would share the "plc_agent" identity and could therefore publish under
# each other's device-level sub-topics (security/agents/plc/<other-device>/#).
# If per-device isolation is required, switch to one MQTT user per physical
# device (e.g. plc_PLC001, plc_PLC002) with the same `topic write
# security/agents/plc/#` rule, and provision a distinct password per device
# instead of the shared MOSQUITTO_AGENT_PASSWORD.

# --- Camera agents: publish only under their own topic prefix ---
user camera_agent
topic write security/agents/camera/#

# --- Drone agents ---
user drone_agent
topic write security/agents/drone/#

# --- Generic IoT agents ---
user iot_agent
topic write security/agents/iot/#

# --- PLC agents ---
user plc_agent
topic write security/agents/plc/#

# --- Robot agents ---
user robot_agent
topic write security/agents/robot/#

# --- Edge gateway: subscribes to all agent telemetry, publishes its own
#     status/health under security/gateway/# ---
user edge_gateway
topic read security/agents/#
topic write security/gateway/#
